          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
            as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundation+of+mathematics"} foundation of mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
            exist.
          %h2#statement Statement
          %h3#in_material_set_theory  In material set theory
          %p
            The
            %strong axiom of union
            states the following:
          .un_defn
            %h6#axiom_union Axiom (union)
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
              is a (material) set, then there exists a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in U
              whenever
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒳
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in B \in \mathcal{X}
          %p
            Using the axiom of separation (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+separation"} bounded separation
            is enough), one can prove the existence of a particular set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            such that the members of the members of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            are the
            %em only
            members of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+extensionality"} axiom of extensionality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is unique; it is usually denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcup\mathcal{X}
            and called the
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            of (the elements of)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
          %p
            A slightly different notation may be used when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            is (Kuratowski)-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"}> finite
            ; for example,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcup\{A,B,C\}
            may be denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cup B \cup C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi k
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B_k \;|\; k \in I)
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+sets"} family of sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcup_{k \in I} B_k
            (and the usual variations for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence"} sequence
            of sets) for
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcup \{B_k \;|\; k \in I\}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+replacement"} axiom of replacement
            to prove that the latter set (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/range"} range
            of the family) exists in general.
          %h3#in_dependent_type_theory  In dependent type theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tarski+universe"} Tarski universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V, \in)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+sets"} pure sets
            which behaves as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊢
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mi V
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:V \vdash \sum_{y:V} y \in x
            %strong axiom of union
            is given by the following
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rule"} inference rule
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} union
                        %mi V
                      %mo :
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi V
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo :
                          %mi V
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo :
                          %mi V
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi z
                          %mo :
                          %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{union}_V:\prod_{x:V} \sum_{U:V} \prod_{y:V} \prod_{z:V} (y \in x) \times (z \in y) \to (z \in U)}
          %p There is a similar axiom for binary unions:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} union
                        %mi V
                      %mo :
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi V
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo :
                          %mi V
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo :
                          %mi V
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi z
                          %mo :
                          %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{union}_V:\prod_{x:V} \prod_{y:V} \sum_{U:V} \prod_{z:V} ((z \in x) \to (z \in U)) \times ((z \in y) \to (z \in U))}
          %p
            With the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theoretic+axiom+of+choice"} type theoretic axiom of choice
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} union
                        %mi V
                      %mo :
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∪
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo :
                          %mi V
                          %mo ×
                          %mi V
                          %mo →
                          %mi V
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi V
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo :
                          %mi V
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi z
                          %mo :
                          %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{union}_V:\sum_{(-) \cup (-):V \times V \to V} \prod_{x:V} \prod_{y:V} \prod_{z:V} ((z \in x) \to (z \in x \cup y)) \times ((z \in y) \to (z \in x \cup y))}
          %h2#related_notions Related notions
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            is given as a collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            of some ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            itself already satisfies the conclusion of the hypothesis (and then bounded separation gives us the union that we want). This is the only case when unions are taken in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structural+set+theory"} structural set theory
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+unions"} disjoint unions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} predicative mathematics
            requires an axiom giving their existence. (In impredicative mathematics, we can construct disjoint unions from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"} power sets
            and
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+products"} cartesian products
          %p
            One could also include
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union+structure"} union structure
            in the set theory.
